A||||2||pHoOl||Changing the water pump||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||10-15-2000||01:50 AM||||Exactly how hard is it to do?  my 88 has been making strange bearing noises and a friend said that he thinks it's the water pump.  I'll take it somewhere to get diagnosed, but what needs to be done to change it?  I thought i remembered hearing that you need to drop the entire engine.  I can only imagine what the dealer would want to charge for that!!<P>thanks for help,<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-15-2000||02:21 AM||||If its a 6 cylinder like in your signature..then its really a simple job. I did my formula all by my lonesome! NO, you do not have to drop the engine...<BR>Basically you loosen the altanator, drop the belt, move a couple of minor things for easy access (like that braket under the thermo housing and battery) and use several different size torx bits to take off the pump. You can do it from the top to...no need to get under the car. Its been a while since I did mine (well, maybe 4 or 5 months), but I do recall it actually being one of the easier things I had to do! Its really NOT AT ALL as hard as you would think!<BR>Now, if its a 4 banger...well, um..I have no idea.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||pHoOl||10-15-2000||02:30 AM||||Nope, it's a v6.  Okay, sounds like it's not that hard, but i'd have to figure out a place to do it.  Since i'm at school, the parking lot might not be the best place to do engine work.  then again, maybe it's a good idea, we all know girls love guys who work on their sports cars in the middle of a parking lot.  Thanks for the info as always.  I love this board<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
